Spec: Application-scoped secure connection broker

Purpose:
  Turn approved application imports into authorized peer streams and private local data attachments.

Owns:
  ./SecureConnections.cs
  ./ISecureConnections.cs

References:
  ./SecurePeerServer.sdd
  ./CallerIdentity.sdd

Must:
  Allow eight seconds for an established peer renewal response under congested relay traffic, while preserving original open deadlines and independent authorization revocation checks.
  Accept an optional trusted scoped route provider for formal connections and distinguish its experimental capability from static endpoints.
  Compose formal connection execution under the same exclusive host lock, identity, server authority and stop lifecycle; preserve experimental APIs.
  Recover both formal and experimental old opens only after acquiring the exclusive state host lock.
  Count schema-eight formal flows together with experimental opens before durable active-flow admission.
  Reject unsupported relay budget/warning limits before an experimental open; declared constraints cannot be silently ignored.
  Resolve only owner-configured peer endpoints and approved import scope; authenticate the expected peer before data.
  Journal operation identity before external open, never recreate an old open and retain closed-after-restart outcomes.
  Hold an exclusive per-state host lock before recovering old opens so parallel Agents cannot invalidate each other's live operations.
  Admit at most `128` streams per caller and `1024` globally and bind one-use data pipes to the actual caller and trusted Agent.
  Close corresponding streams after local review revocation or peer authorization expiry without affecting unrelated connections.
  Expose no keys, arbitrary dial targets or bare TCP data ports to ordinary applications.
  When an authenticated server control client is explicitly supplied, require an exact current lease before peer open and renew it before signed expiry without redialing business data.
  Keep preview and server-authorized peer wire shapes distinct; a failed server-authorized attempt never retries the preview shape.
  Admit explicit relay opens only with a server control client, a reviewed relay-allowing import and an exact immutable Agent-owned loopback route for visitor application/import and publisher device/application/service.
  Link relay lifetime to the owned runtime; keep direct opens on the existing direct-only policy and never silently change paths or replay business data.
  Retain the selected transport in the operation journal and report relay only for explicitly relay-scoped operations; legacy direct operations retain their original result.
  Capture monotonic admission before storage and route lookup and carry the same deadline through server authorization and peer setup using the bounded planner.
  Close raw peer sockets when an opening candidate is cancelled, before TLS disposal can delay resource release.


Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify retained opens, caller scope, host exclusion, restart recovery and SDK data delivery in the direct preview.
  [x] #2 Verify actual SDK data delivery with server-issued leases and renewed unchanged authority without backend redial.
  [x] #3 Verify actual SDK relay delivery through protected frpc runtimes with inner data mTLS, current local/server grants and blocked-stream revocation.
